 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "Primary path",
   "items": [
    "Engineer opens a .hdp; the Design Manager opens a view in its FSM or block-diagram editor, each with Signals / Parameters table pages",
    "Generate goes through EditorContext to generate_unit, which writes <lib>/hdl/<unit>.v or .sv atomically",
    "Layers call only downward: everything outside src/gui runs without Qt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "rose",
   "title": "Trust and safety gates",
   "items": [
    "EditorContext.acquire writes <view>.lck (legacy EDIT_LOCK format); a lock held by another user offers read-only or reset",
    "Protected and downstream libraries, or files without write permission, open read-only",
    "generate_unit keeps a sha256 per file in .hdlstudio_gen.json and refuses to overwrite a hand-edited file unless the user confirms"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "title": "Loading and saving views",
   "items": [
    "load_view uses formats.import_sm / import_bd for legacy files, or FsmView / BlockDiagram .json",
    "A .sm is written back in place by export_sm; other views save as <view>.<kind>.json",
    "Optional .bak copy before save (Main Settings > Save)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "amber",
   "title": "External dependencies",
   "items": [
    "PySide6 (Qt 6) for every window; pyslang is optional, with a regex fallback scanner",
    "HDL Designer edits the same .hdp / .sm / .bd files and honours the same .lck locks",
    "Text files can open in an external editor from Preferences"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "slate",
   "title": "Per-user state",
   "items": [
    "user_prefs.json, session.json, autosave/ and parse caches live in ~/hdl_studio/user/v<YYYY.MM> ($HDLSTUDIO_HOME); a new release copies the newest older folder",
    "Uncaught errors go to stderr, logs/errors.log and the Design Manager Log",
    "Autosave of unsaved editors runs on a timer and is offered for recovery when the view reopens"
   ]
  }
 ]
}